# TypeScript conventions

This project is TypeScript-only Playwright automation. Do not add `.js` test or page files.

## Types

- Prefer `const`. Use `let` only when reassignment is required. Never use `var`.
- Do not use `any`. Use `unknown` at untyped boundaries, then narrow.
- Import types with `import type`. Page methods should declare an explicit `Promise<void>` (or a real return type).

```typescript
import { type Page, type Locator } from '@playwright/test';

export class LoginPage {
  readonly submit: Locator;

  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {
    this.submit = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Sign in' });
  }

  async submitForm(): Promise<void> {
    await this.submit.click();
  }
}
```

## Style

- Named exports for page classes and fixtures. One page class per file.
- No unused imports or unused locals.
- Do not add React, Next.js, or UI-framework patterns. This repo is a test project.
